I think there are a few ideas intertwined here, and one of them is genuinely powerful from an engineering standpoint.

The strongest one is representation independence.

Instead of reasoning directly in one medium (English, code, CAD, mathematics, images), you translate into an intermediate representation where the structure is easier to manipulate, then render back out.

Conceptually:

Natural Language
        │
        ▼
Intent Graph
        │
        ▼
Operator Graph
        │
        ▼
Latent Reasoning Space
        │
        ├────────────┬────────────┬───────────┐
        ▼            ▼            ▼           ▼
Mathematics      Code       Blueprint     Narrative

The latent representation isn’t “English.”

It isn’t “Python.”

It isn’t “physics.”

It is a structural description that can be rendered into any of those.

